                <pb facs="0845" n="757" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg757"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. McCormick to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic">St.
                            Petersburg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1904-08-13"><hi rendition="#italic">August 13,
                        1904</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. McCormick reports that he has communicated the contents of Department’s
                    telegram of the 11th instant to the minister for foreign affairs, and has
                    protested against the condemnation of the cargo of flour carried by the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Arabia;</hi> that the minister stated that he would have
                    to consult with the minister of marine and with a commission which is
                    considering the matter. States that the minister for foreign affairs stated in
                    one of his notes that if this decision should be found unsatisfactory the case
                    could be appealed to the council of the admiralty, which would have final
                    jurisdiction.)</p>
            </div>
